# Dev Doctor project rules

## Continuation

- Read `TOMORROW_RESUME.md` first. It is the canonical, overwrite-in-place continuation file and is marked with the latest update date.
- Inspect the current Git status and relevant implementation before editing.
- Preserve the real adaptive Concierge flow; do not replace it with scripted answers or bypasses.

## Local inference and E2E

- Prefer the configured local LM Studio/OpenAI-compatible runtime and the model profile selected by the run.
- The Number Quest adaptive conversation intentionally has no fixed turn cap. It must continue until the real completion gate is detected or an inference/browser failure occurs.
- Keep `E2E_INFERENCE_TIMEOUT_MS` as the per-inference safety boundary. A timeout prevents a hung request; it does not limit the number of valid conversation turns.
- Completion-gate confirmation must remain explicit and one-time before clicking `Generate GDD / PRD`.

## Validation

- Keep strict downstream contracts and validation enabled.
- Optional enrichment failures may remain non-blocking, but core workflow failures must remain visible.
- Run focused syntax/tests plus build and lint when practical.
- Verify edited files after changes and report any unvalidated local-model run honestly.

## Git and handoff

- Include source, scripts, model profiles, tests, documentation, and this `.clinerules` file in the project commit when they are part of the requested work.
- Do not commit secrets, local environment files, generated dependencies, or transient process logs.
- Update `TOMORROW_RESUME.md` in place after a significant milestone. Mark it `LATEST VERSION` and use the current date.